# Publish finished work

When a request that changes this repo is finished, commit the relevant files and push `main` so GitHub Pages refreshes. Do this at the end of the turn, before the reply.

- Skip the commit when nothing changed, or when the user said not to commit.
- Leave out secrets such as `.env` and credential files.
- If `git push` is rejected because the hourly sync moved `origin/main`, run `git pull --rebase origin main` and push again.
- Never force-push.
